# Review target (`TARGET`)

When suggesting or running live `repolens review` / `sentinel` validation against a dogfood repo (e.g. PatternSorcerer):

- Use **`$TARGET`** for `--path` and **`$TARGET/reports`** for `--out`
- Do not hard-code `/Users/vivek/Development/PatternSorcerer` unless the user explicitly asks
- Confirm `TARGET` is set before running (`echo "$TARGET"`); if unset, ask the user rather than guessing a path

**Speed (do not call these “fast” unless they really are):**

| Intent | Command |
|--------|---------|
| Unit (seconds) | `python -m pytest tests/test_themes.py tests/test_report.py -q` |
| Scanners only | `repolens review --path "$TARGET" --out "$TARGET/reports" --scanners-only` |
| LLM only on delta | `repolens review --path "$TARGET" --out "$TARGET/reports" --changed --deep --timeout 900` |
| Full warm pack (slow on 32B) | omit `--changed` — `auto` with **no fingerprint delta still packs all files** |
| Full audit | `--full-audit` (slowest) |

Typical full-audit:

```bash
repolens review --path "$TARGET" --out "$TARGET/reports" --full-audit --model qwen2.5-coder:32b --verbose --timeout 3600
```
